# iOS / iPadOS shell

`@main`, the composition root, and nothing else. If a file here does anything a test would want to
assert on, it belongs in a package.

## What lives here

- The `App` struct and its `WindowGroup`
- One composition root that builds the dependency container: `liveValue` for the app, and the place
  every `.package(path:)` is wired in
- `Info.plist`, entitlements, asset catalog, `PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy`
- The one place configuration is read — injected onward as `AppEnvironment`, never re-read from a
  feature (CLAUDE.md §2.10)

## What does not

Views, view models, networking, persistence, formatting, business rules. All of it goes in
`Packages/`, because that is where `swift test` can reach it without a simulator.

Adding a screen? `/new-feature`. It creates the package, the route case and the one line here.
